n pandas Problem Description I would like the dtype parameter to be compatible with opening multiple sheets. Feature Description when a list of sheets is passed, dtype could be a dictionary with {elem_on_list: usual_dtype_parameter} so if sheet_name = [0,'Sheet3'] dtype could be dtype={0:{'colA':str, 'colB': 'float64'}, 'Sheet3':{'colA':'datetime64[ns]', 'colB': str} Alternative Solutions Iterate yourself and create the dictionary yourself with Additional Context In my case, pandas automatic decision of what the object is, doesn't work well in my scenarios. It always assumes numbers, even if the column has explicitly been marked as \"text\" in Excel, so I need to ...",
